    "summary": "Lovelight duet + monster Not Fade Away jam make this a classic",
    "blurb": "The set bursts with high‑energy Lovelight featuring Janis Joplin and Pigpen, while the second set delivers a smoking Not Fade Away into Saint Stephen and an inspired Attics Of My Life. Jerry’s guitar is described as sexy and on fire, and Bob shines on the extended jams.",
    "review": "July 16 1970 at San Rafael’s Euphoria Ballroom captured one of the most legendary collaborations in Dead history – Janis Joplin dropping in for a jaw‑dropping Turn On Your Lovelight duet with Ron \"Pigpen\" McKernan. The first set rides that excitement straight into a fiery Candyman and keeps the momentum rolling with classic staples like China Cat Sunflower › I Know You Rider. By the second set the band is locked in: a smoking Not Fade Away jam rockets into Saint Stephen, while Attics Of My Life and Cumberland Blues add high‑octane peaks. Reviewers repeatedly note Jerry Garcia’s “sexy” tone and interplay with Janis, Bob Weir’s top‑form rhythm work on the jams, and Pigpen’s organ growls that anchor the guest spots. The soundboard captures are crisp – from Charlie Miller’s pristine digital transfer to the Clugston tape source – preserving every banter, profanity‑spiked quip (“Aw Fuck!”) and spontaneous spark that made this night mythic.",
